+# TC-v3 · AFTER measurement · the §3.1 obligations and the §3.4 gate
+
+**Unit** OWNER-RULING-2026-09-03-02, client half · merged `#143` → `4d3a4bb` (staging) → `8ef3cf0` (main)
+**Measured** 2026-09-03 · **`src/` NOT edited this turn**
+
+**Provenance of the component under test.** The bundle was built from this working tree, whose four
+client-half files hash byte-identical to `origin/staging`:
+`2f3efff7…` `a08099c8…` `e05aa4c9…` `2b30b3a1…` — the same post-images the Auditor blob-verified
+before landing. **The card measured is the card that shipped.**
+
+---
+
+## 0 · ⚠ CORRECTION — v3 IS on production
+
+The instruction states *"`get_top_contributors_v3` does not exist on production (measured:
+v3_present=false)"* and directs that this be treated as **H-7, a pending apply**.
+
+**Measured by me on `jtdtehuqtinjxropkkcn`, 2026-09-03 15:58:49.322679 UTC:**
+
+```
+v3_present = true
+present    = get_top_contributors_v1, get_top_contributors_v2, get_top_contributors_v3
+```
+
+Signature at **15:59:06.570877 UTC**:
+`TABLE(user_id uuid, rank_position integer, contributor_score integer, recent_score integer)`,
+`STABLE`, `SECURITY DEFINER`, `anon` EXECUTE true. **Exactly the frozen §2.2 shape.**
+
+Either it landed between the Auditor's reading and mine, or the earlier reading was wrong. Either way
+**H-7 should be re-examined rather than left standing** — the register currently carries a blocker
+against a condition that no longer holds. Raised, not resolved; the apply is not D2's to confirm.
+
+**Consequence, in D2's favour and stated plainly:** this made the real production §3.4 reading
+possible, which is what §2 below rests on.
+
+---
+
+## 1 · The progress bar — proved on real production data
+
+`get_top_contributors_v3()` on production, **2026-09-03 15:59:10.224553 UTC**, with both formulas
+computed in SQL:
+
+| rank | name | chars | recent (displayed) | lifetime | **NEW bar** `recent / rank1.recent` | OLD bar `lifetime / rank1.lifetime` |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | Amit Baran Sen | 14 | 7,233 | 9,143 | **100 %** | 100 % |
+| 2 | Mainak Mridha | 13 | 7,055 | 9,551 | **98 %** | **104 %** |
+| 3 | Dipannita Sen | 13 | 6,823 | 11,546 | **94 %** | **126 %** |
+
+**No row exceeds 100 % under the new formula, and the bars descend with the rank.**
+
+The old formula overflows **on two rows today, not one** — 104 % and 126 %. `overflow-hidden` clipped
+both to full, so the second- and third-placed rows rendered as full as the leader, and the *last* row
+was the most emphatic. The 121 % on record was that same defect measured on an earlier day; the
+number moves with the data, the defect did not.
+
+**Why it cannot recur:** rank 1 holds the maximum `recent_score` by construction — the function orders
+by it — so the quotient cannot exceed 1. Verified on staging in the same query
+(`rank1_holds_max_recent = true`, 15:58:45.676292 UTC).
+
+**Rendered bar widths agree with the arithmetic**: `100%` / `98%` / `94%` read off the live DOM in
+every run in §3.
+
+---
+
+## 2 · §3.4 — the displayed numbers descend
+
+**Production data, rendered:** `[7233, 7055, 6823]` → **descending. GATE PASSES.**
+
+And it is discriminating this time. The lifetime figures the card also shows are
+**9,143 / 9,551 / 11,546** — *not* descending, rank 3 holding the largest. Had the card still rendered
+`contributor_score` as its primary figure, the displayed sequence would have been that one, and the
+gate would have failed. On staging both fields are identical (764/509/509), which is why the staging
+render could never have decided this — F-68.
+
+---
+
+## 3 · §3.1 obligations — measured in a real engine
+
+**Instrument.** Production bundle built locally, served from `127.0.0.1:4173`, rendered in Chromium
+(Playwright). **Localhost is in `no_proxy`, so the egress proxy that reset four earlier configurations
+is not in the path at all.** All data is injected by route interception - nothing reached a backend,
+and the build carries the repo's synthetic hermetic Supabase values, never a credential.
+
+**Every run below is SUBSTITUTED**: the numbers are production's, read read-only; the names are
+production's real top three (`PROD-NAMES`) or all replaced with the longest production name eligible
+for the card (`NAME-21` = `Partha Sarathi Moulik`, 21 chars, read 09:18:25.228393 UTC). Staging's
+longest eligible name is **12** — shorter than `Amit Baran Sen` (14) — so staging data cannot
+exercise §3.1 at all.
+
+### 3.1 obligation 1 — rows grow taller · **SATISFIED**
+
+| viewport | card | row height | three rows below the fold? |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| phone 360×800 | **250 × 324 px** | **48 px** each | **No** — `cardExtendsBelowFold: false` |
+| desktop 1280×800 | **258 × 370.66 px** | **48 px** each | **No** |
+
+Identical in `PROD-NAMES` and `NAME-21`. The two-line block did not make the rows taller in any
+harmful way: the 28 px avatar still sets the row's content height, exactly as the pre-build arithmetic
+predicted — and that prediction is now retired as a hypothesis and replaced by a reading.
+
+### 3.1 obligation 2 — long names truncate with an ellipsis · **SATISFIED, and this is the reading jsdom could not produce**
+
+| viewport | mode | name | chars | clientWidth | scrollWidth | **ellipsis active** | `text-overflow` |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| phone 360 | PROD-NAMES | Amit Baran Sen | 14 | 84 | 84 | no | ellipsis |
+| phone 360 | PROD-NAMES | Mainak Mridha | 13 | 79 | 79 | no | ellipsis |
+| phone 360 | PROD-NAMES | Dipannita Sen | 13 | 75 | 75 | no | ellipsis |
+| **phone 360** | **NAME-21** | Partha Sarathi Moulik | **21** | **105** | **115** | **YES** | ellipsis |
+| **phone 360** | **NAME-21** | Partha Sarathi Moulik | **21** | **105** | **115** | **YES** | ellipsis |
+| **phone 360** | **NAME-21** | Partha Sarathi Moulik | **21** | **99** | **115** | **YES** | ellipsis |
+| desktop 1280 | NAME-21 | Partha Sarathi Moulik | 21 | 115 | 115 | no — **it fits** | ellipsis |
+
+`white-space: nowrap`, `overflow: hidden`, `text-overflow: ellipsis` on every row. **It truncates. It
+does not wrap and it does not overflow** — the row height is 48 px in every case, which a wrap would
+have changed.
+
+Row 3 truncates **earlier** (99 px against 105 px) because its secondary line reads `Lifetime 11,546`
+— five digits and a comma — taking more of the right-hand cell. That is the tightest row on the card,
+and it is a row Option B created; worth knowing before a longer name or a six-figure lifetime score
+arrives.
+
+At real desktop width the 21-character name **fits with nothing to spare** (115 = 115). One more
+character truncates there too.
+
+### 3.1 obligation 3 — real mid-range Android · **STILL OWED**
+
+The phone run is Chromium at a 360×800 viewport with a mid-range Android user-agent. **That is an
+emulated viewport, not a device.** Per §3.1 and the D2 standard an emulator is not the gate, so **no
+Android reading exists — neither VERIFIED nor OWNER-ATTESTED.** It must be taken by the Owner on the
+runbook. Nothing above should be read as satisfying it.
+
+---
+
+## 4 · Screenshots
+
+`after-phone-360x800-PROD-NAMES.png` · `after-phone-360x800-NAME-21.png` ·
+`after-desktop-1280x800-PROD-NAMES.png` · `after-desktop-1280x800-NAME-21.png`
+
+**Lane: none.** All four are the locally-built production bundle at `127.0.0.1:4173` with injected
+data — **SUBSTITUTED**, not `staging.50mmretina.com` and not `www.50mmretina.com`. No screenshot in
+this pack came from a deployed lane, and none should be captioned as if it did.
+
+The consent banner is `position: fixed` and covered the card at 360 px. It was **hidden for the
+capture only, after the measurements were taken** — never accepted, never dismissed, no consent
+simulated, and it sits outside the card's flow so the geometry above is unaffected.
+
+## 5 · Status of every line
+
+| class | applies to |
+|---|---|
+| **VERIFIED** | §0 production catalogue readings; §1 both formulas from production data; §2 and §3 geometry, read from a live DOM in a real engine at the stated UTC times |
+| **SUBSTITUTED** | all of §3 — injected data, real component. Proves the CARD, never a lane's data |
+| **NOT MEASURED** | the Android reading (§3.1 obligation 3); any render of a deployed lane |
+
+*D2 · Client & Delivery. No `src/**` change, no SQL, no `supabase/**`, no `docs/gates/**`, no ledger.
+D1's migration is asserted against, never edited.*
